{ "Identifier":           {"ImplementerID": "1", "ImplementationID": "CAE-ASM-V1.0-I01", "AIMName": "1CAE-ASM-V1.0-I01"},
  "Header":               "CAE-ASM-V1.0",

  "APIProfile":           "Basic",
  "Execution":            "Continuous",
  "Description":          "Audio Scene Management: an audio chain - Audio Object Editing, then Audio Scene Editing - and a speech chain - Speech Object Editing, then Speech Scene Editing - whose Scenes Multimodal Scene Editing (OSD-MSE) composes into a Multimodal Scene; each AIM with its own User Command, each returning the User Command with its response (how each action was executed). Every User Command carries the User Point of View and the Object to acquire or deliver, in full or by its name; the Objects and Scenes are named as the User names them. Every edit is a new version in the Module's Shared Storage. Speech Object Editing has a Speech Object translated by Text and Speech Translation (MMC-TST); the translation replaces the original, under its identifier, so every Speech Scene holding it holds the translation, at its place. Capture, reading the User's stored Objects, and hearing the Objects and Scenes - Audio and Speech Object Delivery - are the User Agent's, through the Units of its Physical Layer. The User Commands reach the editing AIMs on the Ports of the Composite, which the User Agent addresses by Data Type and Port Number, so that the Controller, and only the Controller, decides which of the editing AIMs a User Command reaches. A person may also speak the User Commands: Voice Command Interface (MMC-VCI), which MMC specifies, takes the speech, forms the User Command that the person asks for - from the commands of this Module, which it knows from the Access of the Module - issues it to the editing AIMs, takes the response of each, and answers the person aloud and as text; it also gives the text it heard.",

